From 814b28736ee48068ac62b71f138590b0f957e178 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jaxdad <atxhxag@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 16:14:53 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] feat(headless): add a display-less RDP client for
 WebAssembly hosts

`ironrdp-headless` builds to `wasm32-wasip1` and runs one RDP session per
`run` call, with the host owning the network: the host opens TCP, upgrades
to TLS when asked (and verifies the certificate), and moves bytes through
four imports (`tessera.recv`, `send`, `upgrade_tls`, `event`). This lets a
server keep an RDP session open while no viewer is attached.

The module runs the connection sequence and CredSSP (NTLM, no network
client), the session including the Deactivation-Reactivation Sequence,
keyboard, mouse, wheel and Unicode input through `ironrdp_input::Database`,
resize through Display Control, Suppress Output and full-redraw requests.
H.264 pictures go to the host undecoded through the presenting-decoder
hook; other updates are reported as RGBA regions of the composited image.
The server's auto-reconnect cookie stays inside the module, and a later run
can present it to rejoin the same session.

The host-facing byte formats live in `wire` and have unit tests.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
